+# Agent Session Record export
+
+Use `/export agent-session [directory]` to export the current chat as ASR 0.1.
+For saved legacy transcripts, use:
+
+```sh
+qwen sessions export --format agent-session --session SESSION_ID
+qwen sessions export --format agent-session --input transcript.jsonl --output ./exports
+```
+
+One selected session writes to stdout. A new output directory receives private
+files with hashed names. `--since` filters by source modification time.
+Explicit input files need no model or account login.
+
+The export preserves retained text, reasoning and tool results. It declares
+missing approvals, model-call boundaries, usage and other unavailable facts.
+Managed journals are rejected. Corrupt lines and partial tails produce gaps.
+Known credentials are removed, but review all exports before sharing them.
